  "body": "The machine limit check judges a touch probe's catalog `rpm` against the mounted machine's spindle range, so every probing program on a machine that states a minimum spindle speed is refused at post:\n\n```\npost blocked - machine Tormach 770MX: 1 limit problem(s): Probe X face: tool T99 Probe runs 1 rpm, below the machine's 175\n```\n\nFound while preparing the #521 hands-on probe test: catalog `PRB-0400` with the built-in Tormach 770MX (spindle 175-10000 rpm), Tormach PathPilot post.\n\n**Cause:** `crates/app/src/machine/mod.rs` (~189-198) checks `tool.rpm` against `spindle_min`/`spindle_max` for every op, as the comment says (\"today every op posts its tool's rpm\"). A probe posts no speed at all: `posting.rs` forces rpm 0 for `ToolKind::Probe`, and #523/#526 posts no spindle start for it. So the probe's rpm field is never commanded, and judging it is a false refusal.\n\n**Fix:** skip the spindle-range clause for probe tools (`ToolKind::Probe`), and for any op whose posted rpm is 0. Keep every other limit (axis travel, feeds) judged for probe moves.\n\nDone means: a Probe op with the catalog probe posts on the Tormach 770MX (and any machine with a stated spindle minimum) with no limit problem, while a cutter below the minimum is still refused. Pinned by a machine-check test.\n",
